version.  The licence text is in COPYING.  The source files are unmodified;
the files listed below are the only ones that were added or removed.

Changes
-------
Added:
  config/tm-uclinux.h   target description: 68000, uClinux, Motorola operand
                        syntax read by user/cc/as.c.  Derived from
                        config/tm-news.h (operand/prologue/epilogue macros)
                        and config/tm-m68k.h (included; calling convention,
                        alignment and registers are kept so that code is
                        compatible with the C library built by gcc 2.95).
  README.uclinux       this file

Removed (build products of the documentation, regenerated by makeinfo/TeX):
  *.info*, *.dvi, *.aux, *.cps, *.fns, gcc.hlp, c-parse.output
  The texinfo sources and the pre-generated parsers (c-parse.tab.c, cexp.c)
  are kept, so neither bison nor makeinfo is needed.

How it is built
---------------
user/cc/gcc.mk builds, from this unmodified source:
  cc1  and  cpp (cccp)   for the Mac (m68k-elf-gcc, -Os, flat binaries)
  cc1-host, cpp-host     32-bit host copies, only used to test the build
The generators (genconfig ...) run on the host.  The usual `configure'
symbolic links (tm.h, config.h, md, aux-output.c) are replaced by files in
the build directory.  See user/cc/build-in-container.sh.

Usage notes
-----------
* cc1 only knows plain identifiers inside __attribute__ ((...)).  The libc
  headers installed on the Mac get `#define __attribute__(x)' appended to
  features.h (user/cc/build.sh).
* GCC 1.42 does not know __restrict, __restrict__ and __extension__; the
  cc driver passes -D shims for them.
* `-g' is not supported: DBX output is disabled in tm-uclinux.h.
